        path "debian/**",
        path "distro/**",
        path "services/lege-sessiond/**",
        path "shell/lege-shell/**"
    ]
    intent """
        Integration choices the user made on 2026-09-03, revised later the same day. (a) Terminal: ProviderRole::Terminal, exclusive, candidates from TerminalEmulator desktop entries, default kitty; the shell relays the selection with lege_shell_manager_v1.set_terminal and answers terminal_requested by launching the provider through the launch chain; Super+grave (compositor chord; a bare ~ or ` is a typed character and cannot be a global chord) toggles the terminal: launch when none, unshelve/activate when shelved or unfocused, shelve and refocus the previous window when focused, never close. No Ctrl+Alt+T. 'Open terminal here' in the Files context menu launches it with --directory. /etc/xdg/kitty/kitty.conf shipped by legeos-shell with the LegeOS palette, background_opacity 0.85, remember_window_size no, wayland_titlebar_color system, overridable by ~/.config/kitty. (b) Files object: secondary-click menu on rows and empty space reusing surface/context_menu.rs and the declared files.* verbs (Open, Open with…, Open terminal here, Copy path, Rename, Move to trash, Properties; New folder, Paste, Select all, Sort by…, Show hidden), then multi-select, keyboard verbs, drag-and-drop and properties-as-pane. (c) Search: the top field on Home stays the application launcher only (COSMIC's launcher shape); real search is the Files object's search field expanded into a partial-screen panel (about two thirds of the field, centred, hairline edge) over lege-filed's scoped index with path, size and modified time per row and keyboard navigation, whose last row is 'Search everywhere with FSearch'; ProviderRole::FileSearch, exclusive, launched with --search <query>; 'Search here…' in the context menu. The later indexing direction replaces the interim two-database arrangement: lege-filed owns one persistent, incrementally maintained derived file index used by integrated Files search, a remote-index FSearch fork, Silvaview-rs, the CLI and future clients.
        """
    note """
        The application-integration plan remains docs/planning/window-groups-and-application-integration.md for terminal, Files UI and provider work. Its section 4.2 statements that fsearch keeps a second database and Files.Search1 is not replaced are superseded by the user's later 2026-09-03 direction and docs/planning/shared-incremental-file-index.md. The detailed implementation is tracked by @legeos.work.shared-incremental-file-index.
        """
    depends_on [ @legeos.work.wayland-clipboard-and-dnd-transport ]
    implements [ @legeos.decision.the-home-field-is-a-launcher-not-a-search ]
    part_of [ @legeos.work.home-surface-usability-next ]
    supersedes [ @legeos.work.application-integration-interim/1 ]
}

record legeos.work.build-set-archive-verification/1 : work {
    title "D2 — BuildSetId feeds debian/changelog, the local archive verifies whole sets, and the image can consume a published set"
    state proposed
    scope [
        path "ci/**",
        path "cli/lege/src/dev/repo.rs",
        path "crates/lege-build/**",
        path "debian/changelog",
        path "debian/rules",
        path "distro/apt/**",
        path "tools/xtask/src/archive.rs",
        path "tools/xtask/src/build_set.rs",
        path "tools/xtask/src/signatures.rs"
    ]
    intent """
        Make the BuildSetId the one version authority (generate the debian/changelog head entry from it for source builds), add `lege dev repo verify` (one id across the set, no missing component against components.toml, valid InRelease/Release.gpg, previous set still installable), give the archive a staged/candidate marker distinct from the boot-deployment candidate vocabulary, record provenance (toolchain, host, Ubuntu index time), add a disposable Ubuntu 26.04 source-build lane under ci/ that reports not-executed when mmdebstrap/podman are absent, and provide the mkosi drop-in that points the image at a named published set.
        """
    note """
        HEAD reconciliation 2026-09-03: BuildSetId, keep-3 pruning, signing and mixed-set rejection already exist (crates/lege-build, cli/lege/src/dev/repo.rs); debian/changelog carries an independent 0.1.0~dev1; no verify command, no clean-root lane, no local-snapshot consumption by just image.
        """
    acceptance {
        check archive-verify {
            statement """
                `lege dev repo verify` detects a mixed set, a missing component and a bad signature in fixtures, and reports the current and previous sets as installable.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege repo"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.de01-integrated-gate-20260904 ]
        }
        check image-drop-in {
            statement """
                A documented mkosi drop-in makes `just image` consume a named published set from the local archive (or the drop-in is documented as not exercised because mkosi is absent).
                """
            method manual
        }
        check one-version-authority {
            statement """
                The debian/changelog head entry used by the source build is derived from the BuildSetId; a test proves the derivation and `just deb-plan` prints the same id.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-build && just deb-plan"
            verified_by [
                @legeos.evidence.de01-integrated-gate-20260904,
                @legeos.evidence.de01-version-authority-20260904
            ]
        }
    }
    implements [ @legeos.decision.debian-packaging ]
    part_of [
        @legeos.milestone.developer-edition-0-1,
        @legeos.work.deployment-activation-and-resourced
    ]
}

record legeos.work.compositor-window-authority/1 : work {
    title "The compositor's window authority: typed layers, one scene, explicit minimisation, recovery without the shell"
    state completed
    scope [ path "compositor/**", path "crates/lege-window/**", path "interfaces/wayland/**" ]
    intent """
        Make lege-window the thing that decides stacking and geometry rather than a set of helpers: typed overlay layers as a total order with rules about which client may claim which layer; the one-workspace invariant as a type-level property, with deterministic migration when an output is removed and validation of restored geometry against the current topology; explicit minimisation to a Window Shelf that is always restorable to a recoverable geometry; a compositor-owned recovery band, a show-all-windows scatter and an escape route out of fullscreen that all work when the shell is dead; drag anchors held in one global logical coordinate space across mixed-scale outputs; window commands gated on activation grants with recent-input evidence; and property tests over generated multi-output topologies. lege-comp-integration keeps the render thread off D-Bus, hardens the identity cache against PID reuse, and tells the governor which instance the user is looking at.
        """
    part_of [ @legeos.milestone.m1-session-runtime ]
}

record legeos.work.consumers-cli-portal-shell/1 : work {
    title "The clients: the CLI over the whole OS, one portal backend, the Home Surface model, Settings"
    state completed
    scope [
        path "apps/lege-settings/**",
        path "cli/lege/**",
        path "crates/lege-client/src/sdk.rs",
        path "portals/**",
        path "shell/**"
    ]
    intent """
        Make the services reachable: lege as one command line over identity, launching, associations with an explanation, files and operations, resources, history with undo, providers, settings, projects, power and updates; xdg-desktop-portal-lege as the single backend implementing FileChooser over the shared last-directory answer, OpenURI and AppChooser over the association broker, Settings and Background over providers and autostart, so a sandboxed application and a normal one behave the same; the Home Surface as a data model over the services (drawers, dock grouping by canonical AppId, the window shelf, the operations drawer) rendered without a toolkit for now; and lege-settings as pages that map one-to-one onto D-Bus interfaces, with nothing a private implementation detail. Everything the shell shows must be available through lege as well.
        """
    after [
        @legeos.work.compositor-window-authority,
        @legeos.work.governor-containment,
        @legeos.work.host-update-transaction,
        @legeos.work.sessiond-persistence-and-launch
    ]
    part_of [ @legeos.milestone.m1-session-runtime ]
}

record legeos.work.deployment-activation-and-resourced/1 : work {
    title "WS6 — build identity, local archive, lege dev deploy, compatibility gates, and replay-gated resourced improvements"
    state proposed
    scope [
        path "cli/lege/**",
        path "crates/lege-build/**",
        path "crates/lege-field/**",
        path "crates/lege-state/**",
        path "debian/**",
        path "distro/**",
        path "docs/adr/**",
        path "interfaces/**",
        path "justfile",
        path "scripts/reinstall-legeos-desktop.sh",
        path "services/lege-boot-health/**",
        path "services/lege-hostd/**",
        path "services/lege-resourced/**",
        path "session/units/**",
        path "tools/xtask/**"
    ]
    intent """
        Tracks A-E, landing order A1 A2 A3 A4 B1 B2 B3 E0 C1 C2 B4 E1 E5 E6 D1 D2 E2 E3 E4 C3. Track A: BuildSetId is the Debian version (0.1.0~dev<epoch>+g<sha7>[.dirty]) across all 13 packages via cargo xtask build-set, which rejects mixed sets; every long-lived process writes a runtime build stamp file at startup (filesystem-first because comp and shell serve no D-Bus; not RuntimeDirectory=, which would delete siblings' stamps); distro/deploy/components.toml is the machine-readable component matrix; lege dev status computes installed-versus-running convergence; doctor gains BuildSetCoherent and RunningMatchesInstalled with PackageAgesConsistent as the documented fallback. Track B: a local signed APT repo at /var/lib/legeos/devrepo (apt-ftparchive + per-developer gpg key, keep=3 sets), one transactional apt-get install --allow-downgrades per set, lege dev rollback as the same path, and an activation engine with per-component rules — shell restart with health gate, apps at next launch, resourced controlled restart, sessiond/filed/portal only when the compatibility gates pass (shipped manual until the composed-session restart test exists), hostd blocked mid-transaction, compositor always needs-session, kernel/boot needs-reboot — ending in the convergence report with the previous set retained. Track C: xtask interface-baseline/check-interface-signatures turns the frozen-signature convention into an enforced gate; lege-state gains schema_meta with min_reader_version, an open()-time refusal of too-new databases, VACUUM INTO snapshots, and the documented one-rollback-generation policy; lege-field gains a document migration registry applied at the load boundary with DocumentTooNew never overwriting. Track D: lege-boot-health calls MarkGood/Rollback itself, and hostd's reconcile_boot wires the GRUB tries counter; cryptographic verification and the hardware matrix stay explicitly deferred. Track E, all gated behind the E0 replay harness (replay recorded traces through Governor::decide with a round-trip fidelity test): thresholds scale with MemTotal (reserve clamp 6.25% 768MiB-4GiB, critical clamp 2% 256MiB-1.5GiB, reproducing today's constants at 48GiB), unsaved-work gains a producer and a TTL via additive SetInstanceWork, richer safe-to-sacrifice signals via additive SetInstanceActivity (idle age, project importance, checkpoint freshness reaching scoring for the first time, user pin as strong weight never hard exclusion), Governor::plan returns multi-step reclaim plans (Elevated trims up to three, Severe throttles top-K to the deficit, Critical stays single-victim) with the foreground structurally excluded at Severe unless demonstrably the runaway, protect.rs stops lowering memory.low and covers sessiond and filed, and ADR-0014 settles systemd-oomd ownership (armed backstop on app.slice at 90%, off on session.slice, avoid on the five session units).
        """
    note """
        Verified corrections folded in: MSRV is 1.97 workspace-wide per ADR-0008 (debian/control, packaging/README.md and CLAUDE.md prose are stale and get the three-line fix); protect.rs currently lowers protection every tick; has_unsaved_work has no producer at ObserveOnly; the health-to-promotion loop is open on both boot backends. Terminate stays unreachable and no phase raises a resourced stage; hand-authored fixture traces prove the harness and properties, not real-world calibration. Settled: per-developer signing key framed as built-on-this-machine; Build1 interface deferred; user pins persisted in sessiond; foreground-runaway thresholds are declared guesses; greeter/DM matrix row ships manual and disabled.
        """
    acceptance {
        check convergence-report {
            statement """
                lege dev deploy ends with a per-component report (build set, needs-session, needs-reboot), a schema-compatibility verdict, and the previous set named for rollback; lege dev status agrees with the stamps.
                """
            method manual
        }
        check protect-never-lowers {
            statement """
                protect.rs writes memory.low only when the desired value exceeds the current one, and covers lege-sessiond and lege-filed.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-resourced protect"
        }
        check replay-fidelity {
            statement """
                Replaying a recorded trace with the config that recorded it reproduces its recorded decisions, and every E1-E4 change quotes its replay diff against the fixture traces.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-resourced replay"
        }
        check rollback-acceptance {
            statement """
                With lege-shell deliberately broken, the set is rejected or health-gated before logout, and lege dev rollback restores the previous set without rebuilding.
                """
            method manual
        }
        check signature-gate {
            statement """
                check-interface-signatures passes on the committed baseline and fails when a shipped argument type is edited in place.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo run -q -p xtask -- check-interface-signatures"
        }
    }
    derived_from [ @legeos.assessment.hotfixability-current-state-20260831 ]
    part_of [ @legeos.work.design-consolidation-roadmap ]
}

record legeos.work.deployment-rollback-completion/1 : work {
    title "D5 — persisted deployment identities, bounded retention, snapshot before userspace mutation, and one diagnostic naming every set and deployment"
    state proposed
    scope [
        path "cli/lege/src/dev/**",
        path "cli/lege/src/main.rs",
        path "distro/deploy/components.toml",
        path "services/lege-boot-health/**",
        path "services/lege-hostd/src/**",
        path "services/lege-hostd/tests/**"
    ]
    intent """
        Assign and persist previous/current/known-good deployment identities; add restart tests for Trial→Promoted/RolledBack; replace the fabricated zero deployment size with a real estimate and bounded retention that never drops the known-good or booted deployment; classify disk exhaustion during Staging; snapshot the root subvolume before a userspace apt install when on Btrfs and show it in `lege dev deploy --dry-run`; add a broken-sessiond fixture to the activation gate; and one status section naming installed set, running set, rollback set, root snapshot, booted deployment and known-good deployment.
        """
    note """
        HEAD reconciliation 2026-09-03: the phase machine, journal and resume are tested for Downloading/Staging/Verifying/AwaitingReboot; userspace and boot rollback are already separate paths; previous_deployment is declared but never assigned; retention trims with a fabricated 0 size.
        """
    acceptance {
        check dry-run-names-everything {
            statement """
                `lege dev deploy --dry-run` and the status section name the installed, running and rollback sets, the root snapshot, the booted and the known-good deployment; the live rollback, logout and reboot remain user-run.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege dev::"
            verified_by [
                @legeos.evidence.de01-deploy-dry-run-20260904,
                @legeos.evidence.de01-integrated-gate-20260904
            ]
        }
        check identities-persist {
            statement """
                previous, current and known-good deployment identities survive a hostd restart and a resume from the Trial phase promotes or rolls back correctly.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-hostd"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.de01-integrated-gate-20260904 ]
        }
        check retention-and-disk {
            statement """
                Retention keeps N deployments but never the known-good or booted one, and disk exhaustion during Staging is a classified failure with the previous set named.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-hostd storage"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.de01-integrated-gate-20260904 ]
        }
    }
    implements [
        @legeos.decision.boot-deploy-secure-boot,
        @legeos.decision.one-privileged-host-daemon
    ]
    part_of [
        @legeos.milestone.developer-edition-0-1,
        @legeos.work.deployment-activation-and-resourced
    ]
}

record legeos.work.design-consolidation-roadmap/1 : work {
    title "Design consolidation roadmap — subtraction, one Files object, federated omnibox, semantic projects, app variants, activation system"
    state proposed
    scope [
        path "cli/lege/**",
        path "crates/lege-appd/**",
        path "crates/lege-associationd/**",
        path "crates/lege-field/**",
        path "crates/lege-session-core/**",
        path "crates/lege-state/**",
        path "crates/lege-types/**",
        path "debian/**",
        path "distro/**",
        path "interfaces/**",
        path "services/lege-boot-health/**",
        path "services/lege-hostd/**",
        path "services/lege-resourced/**",
        path "services/lege-sessiond/**",
        path "shell/lege-shell/**",
        path "tools/xtask/**"
    ]
    intent """
        Carry out the six workstreams of the approved 2026-09-01 consolidation plan (plan file: recursive-crunching-boot). WS1 Home presentation subtraction: shape-aware representation floors, the eight drawers collapse into one adaptive Files object, App tiles only when pinned, conditional LIVE/PARKED. WS2 adaptive Files surface and federated omnibox: HomeSurfaceScreen retired, one persistent FilesSurfaceState across every rung, one search control federating apps, projects, files and actions. WS3 chrome reduction and spatial continuity: per-rung chrome replacing the 34px band, expansion animating from the tile's place. WS4 project semantics: Projects1 extended additively (Describe, ListDetailed, Update, current, state, AddLogicalApp), priority_boost replaced by ProjectImportance feeding SetInstanceHints. WS5 logical app and variant identity: AppId is the variant id, LogicalAppId is new, provenance and trust tiers recorded, flatpak import collision fixed via resolve-through-alias, variant-keyed rights with trust gates. WS6 deployment activation and resourced: BuildSetId as the Debian version, runtime build stamps, component matrix, local signed APT repo, lege dev deploy with pre-activation interface/schema gates, boot-health promotion loop closed, and resourced improved behind a trace-replay harness (scaled thresholds, unsaved-work freshness, richer signals, reclaim plans, memory.low fixes, oomd ownership ADR).
        """
    note """
        User decisions 2026-09-01: all six workstreams in full detail; Settings GUI proceeds in parallel; full Home subtraction; full activation tool in the first iteration with Btrfs boot deployments as the later lane. Sequencing: WS1 → WS2 → WS3, then WS4/WS5 (WS5's types precede WS4's consumption), with WS6 parallel throughout. Ordering within WS6: A1 A2 A3 A4 B1 B2 B3 E0 C1 C2 B4 E1 E5 E6 D1 D2 E2 E3 E4 C3.
        """
    derived_from [ @legeos.assessment.hotfixability-current-state-20260831 ]
    implements [ @legeos.decision.representation-ladder-is-the-organizing-principle ]
    part_of [ @legeos.work.home-field ]
    source {
        kind external
        role origin
        document "design-review-home-and-platform-20260901"
        use """
            The six workstreams and their sequencing follow the review's 'What I would change first' list, verified and elaborated by three plan agents on 2026-09-01.
            """
    }
}

record legeos.work.desktop-validation-foundations/1 : work {
    title "Desktop validation foundations — honest hardware, composed-session, installation and visual gates"
    state active
    scope [
        path ".github/**",
        path "apps/lege-greeter/**",
        path "ci/**",
        path "cli/lege/**",
        path "compositor/**",
        path "scripts/**",
        path "services/lege-boot-health/**",
        path "services/lege-hostd/**",
        path "services/lege-sessiond/**",
        path "shell/**",
        path "tests/**"
    ]
    intent """
        Turn the audit's false-green and manual-only desktop checks into executable gates before treating M2 as a usable session: run the hardware matrix honestly, isolate runtime smoke state, prove compositor/session readiness, automate a nested composed-session journey, exercise the greeter protocol end to end, install every desktop package in a clean root, and compare deterministic Home renders.
        """
    note """
        User-set order on 2026-08-27: complete validation foundations first, then finish the ordinary desktop surfaces; real-hardware execution and its detailed matrix are deliberately deferred to a later Plan-mode session.
        """
    acceptance {
        check clean-install {
            statement """
                CI builds every Debian package and installs the complete desktop set into a clean disposable root or VM, then checks unit binaries, session entries and package coherence.
                """
            method command
            command "tests/integration/package-install.sh"
        }
        check greeter-integration {
            statement """
                A fake greetd server and the real greeter protocol/client exercise success, authentication failure, retry, cancellation, selected session command, and compositor --exec exit propagation.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-greeter && tests/integration/greeter.sh"
        }
        check hardware-runner {
            statement """
                lege doctor --hardware parses the TOML matrix, filters by detected/requested profile and optional check ID, reports each step/expectation without executing destructive actions implicitly, and differs structurally from ordinary doctor.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege doctor::hardware"
        }
        check isolated-smoke {
            statement """
                The integration smoke uses isolated HOME/XDG directories and a private session bus, starts real session services where applicable, and cannot import developer-host desktop state.
                """
            method command
            command "tests/integration/run.sh"
        }
        check nested-session-journey {
            statement """
                An automated nested journey starts compositor, services and shell, observes their readiness, launches a client, exercises input/window/Home recovery including shell restart, and leaves no processes or sockets behind.
                """
            method command
            command "tests/integration/nested-session.sh"
        }
        check readiness-is-honest {
            statement """
                Boot-health cannot report a healthy session unless compositor-active and session-healthy have both been reported; the smoke asserts expected health outcomes instead of accepting any report-only output.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-boot-health -p lege-hostd -p lege-sessiond"
        }
        check visual-regression {
            statement """
                Deterministic Home renders at representative sizes and scale/layout states are compared semantically or pixel-wise against reviewed baselines, with an explicit baseline-update command.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-shell visual_regression"
        }
    }
    derived_from [ @legeos.assessment.desktop-test-readiness-20260827/1 ]
    part_of [ @legeos.milestone.m2-session-runs/1 ]
}

record legeos.work.developer-edition-daily-driver/1 : work {
    title "X1 — a usable FileChooser, an OpenURI portal, the portal in the nested session, and an auditable daily-driver capability matrix"
    state proposed
    scope [
        path "docs/planning/daily-driver-matrix.md",
        path "portals/xdg-desktop-portal-lege/**",
        path "scripts/nested-session.sh",
        path "tests/integration/nested-session.sh"
    ]
    intent """
        In the mid-plan's priority order: make the native FileChooser usable for browser upload and download (full scrolling listing, hidden toggle, request filters, save-as filename, start folder from Recents1); add org.freedesktop.impl.portal.OpenURI resolving through Associations1 and claim it in legeos.portal; document Flatpak portal selection; audit clipboard, media, suspend, keys, removable storage, secrets and MIME into docs/planning/daily-driver-matrix.md with automated/manual/blocked per row; message package needs to the package-selection lane and manual cases to the hardware lane; start the portal in both nested-session harnesses so the user can run a journey.
        """
    note """
        HEAD reconciliation 2026-09-03: FileChooser/AppChooser/Background are native Pixelkit dialogs in the portal process (the 2026-08-27 NoUiAvailable finding is stale) but the file dialog shows ten entries per directory; OpenURI is absent though the docs claim it; clipboard transport is real in the shell; no harness starts the portal.
        """
    acceptance {
        check capability-matrix {
            statement """
                docs/planning/daily-driver-matrix.md marks each of the nine daily-driver areas automated, manual or blocked with its package or provider need, and claims no hardware evidence.
                """
            method manual
        }
        check portal-model-tests {
            statement """
                The dialog model lists every directory entry, applies request filters, and OpenURI resolves the default handler through Associations1, all without a display.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p xdg-desktop-portal-lege"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.de01-integrated-gate-20260904 ]
        }
        check user-journey {
            statement """
                The user completes a browser upload and download, opens an external URL and a downloaded file, and plays media in a LegeOS session.
                """
            method manual
        }
    }
    implements [ @legeos.decision.flatpak-and-crash-handling ]
    part_of [
        @legeos.milestone.developer-edition-0-1,
        @legeos.work.desktop-validation-foundations
    ]
}

record legeos.work.developer-edition-package-closure/1 : work {
    title "D1 — one package-selection declaration drives the seeds, the image list, the metapackages and a closure report"
    state proposed
    scope [
        path "distro/base.toml",
        path "distro/image/compose.sh",
        path "distro/image/mkosi.conf",
        path "distro/image/mkosi.conf.d/**",
        path "distro/metapackages/**",
        path "distro/seeds/**",
        path "tools/xtask/src/main.rs",
        path "tools/xtask/src/seeds.rs"
    ]
    intent """
        Replace the flat seed lists, the hand-maintained 10-packages-base.conf list and the hand-written metapackage control.in files with one declaration (distro/seeds/selection.toml: layers bootstrap/hardware/graphics/session/desktop/browser/media/dev-rust/dev-cuda/opt-a11y/opt-ime/opt-bluetooth, a reason per direct package, role providers, the no-snap conflict). `cargo xtask seeds` generates 50-seeds.conf and the metapackage control files (adding legeos-dev-rust and legeos-dev-cuda) and emits a closure report (direct, transitive, installed size, recommends, missing packages, duplicate providers) against the host's Ubuntu 26.04 indexes with the observation time recorded; check-packaging fails when the generated output and the checked-in files differ.
        """
    note """
        HEAD reconciliation 2026-09-03: compose.sh iterates only minimal/session/desktop/hardware/ime/a11y so dev.seed is never consumed; legeos-session-meta omits legeos-boot-health; no closure tooling, no CUDA selection, no snapshot identity. Recommends are hard-off in the deploy path but on in the image; a --no-recommends image experiment is documented, not applied blindly.
        """
    acceptance {
        check closure-report {
            statement """
                `cargo xtask seeds closure` reports direct and transitive packages, installed size, recommends, missing packages and duplicate providers for the Developer Edition layers, naming the Ubuntu index observation time or stating that resolution was unavailable.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo run -q -p xtask -- seeds closure"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.de01-package-closure-unavailable-20260904 ]
        }
        check generated-not-maintained {
            statement """
                50-seeds.conf, the base package drop-in and every metapackage control file are generated from distro/seeds/selection.toml, and `cargo xtask seeds --check` fails when the checked-in files drift from the declaration.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo run -q -p xtask -- seeds --check"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.de01-seeds-generated-20260904 ]
        }
        check image-consumes-closure {
            statement """
                `just image summary` consumes exactly the generated package list (or records that mkosi is absent on this host).
                """
            method command
            command "just image summary"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.de01-image-summary-mkosi-absent-20260904 ]
        }
    }
    implements [
        @legeos.decision.debian-packaging,
        @legeos.decision.flatpak-and-crash-handling,
        @legeos.decision.mkosi-images
    ]
    part_of [ @legeos.milestone.developer-edition-0-1 ]
}

record legeos.work.display-manager-session-startup-reliability/1 : work {
    title "Make the installed LegeOS display-manager session start deterministically and fail back cleanly"
    state superseded
    scope [
        path "compositor/lege-comp/**",
        path "docs/testing/README.md",
        path "services/lege-filed/**",
        path "services/lege-resourced/**",
        path "session/**",
        path "tests/**"
    ]
    intent """
        Repair the installed-session contract exposed by the 2026-08-22 SDDM attempts: eliminate inherited-display backend selection, make compositor readiness real, start the graphical shell on its trusted socket, end the session when the compositor cannot run, and prevent auxiliary services from exhausting resources during login.
        """
    acceptance {
        check aux-services-bounded {
            statement """
                The resource governor no longer self-aborts after mlockall and the file service's default startup indexing has an explicit finite admission bound exercised by tests.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-resourced -p lege-filed"
        }
        check installed-login {
            statement """
                After rebuilding and installing the packages, selecting LegeOS in SDDM reaches the graphical Home Surface instead of freezing the greeter or leaving a black screen.
                """
            method manual
        }
        check startup-contract {
            statement """
                Automated session/unit tests prove the installed entry forces the hardware backend, publishes deterministic public and trusted-shell sockets, waits for actual compositor readiness, starts lege-shell --surface, and tears down the target if the compositor exits.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-session -p lege-comp && cargo run -q -p xtask -- check-packaging"
        }
    }
    implements [ @legeos.decision.session-greeter-lock/2 ]
    part_of [ @legeos.milestone.m2-session-runs/1 ]
}

