}

record legeos.work.filed-transactions/1 : work {
    title "The file service: journalled transactions, trash, storage reserve, recents, search"
    state completed
    scope [
        path "crates/lege-client/src/proxies/files.rs",
        path "crates/lege-state/src/migrations/files.rs",
        path "interfaces/dbus/org.legeos.Files.*.xml",
        path "services/lege-filed/**"
    ]
    intent """
        Make lege-filed the owner of file state rather than the file manager: survey/plan split so conflict and ordering rules are testable without a filesystem; idempotent journalled steps (copy to a temporary in the destination directory, flush file and directory entry, verify by size or CRC-32 read-back, expose atomically, delete the source last) with resume-after-crash; same-device moves as one rename; conflict policy decided once at plan time; undo planned at commit time for rename, move and trash while delete stays irreversible; the freedesktop trash with the per-volume fallback; volumes, the mount table and the reserve kept for logging in, updating and recovering; recents and the one shared last-directory answer; a name-and-metadata search index with saved queries; and the path actions that are otherwise a service menu.
        """
    part_of [ @legeos.milestone.m1-session-runtime ]
}

record legeos.work.full-distribution-roadmap/1 : work {
    title "Ubuntu-derived full distribution and latest-stable kernel roadmap"
    state proposed
    intent """
        Turn the LegeOS desktop/session and existing distro scaffold into a supportable amd64 Ubuntu 26.04
        binary derivative: clean source builds, signed overlay archive, reproducible image and live installer,
        safe in-series updates, recovery, security operations, hardware qualification, and a LegeOS-owned
        latest-qualified-stable kernel lane. Linux release candidates remain experimental and Ubuntu's signed
        GA kernel remains a rescue path until the independent kernel/driver/signing pipeline is proven.
        """
    note """
        The planning baseline and estimates are in docs/planning/ubuntu-derived-full-distribution-roadmap.md.
        This work proposes replacing the current ADR-0007 kernel posture; a normative superseding ADR and a
        resolved Secure Boot decision are explicit Phase 0 prerequisites, not silently implied here.
        """
}

record legeos.work.governor-containment/1 : work {
    title "The resource governor: a served interface, applied protection, a staged containment ladder and recorded traces"
    state completed
    scope [
        path "distro/policy/**",
        path "interfaces/dbus/org.legeos.Resources1.xml",
        path "services/lege-resourced/**"
    ]
    intent """
        Give lege-resourced everything it needs to act without giving it the ability to act prematurely: serve org.legeos.Resources1 on a task separate from the sampling loop; populate the managed-instance map from the app.slice scan so an action can reach a real cgroup at all; apply memory.oom.group to application cgroups and a modest memory.low to session-critical units (never memory.min, whose hard protection can itself force OOM); implement the observe-only → trim → throttle → checkpoint → terminate ladder, defaulting to observe-only, with an action above the current stage decided, logged and signalled as unapplied; record bounded JSONL traces complete enough for a human to review a decision before enabling enforcement; return a victim-score breakdown so the choice is explainable; distinguish storage, GPU-reset and kernel-lockup stalls from application memory pressure rather than blaming an application; and keep SQLite and fsync off the loop entirely.
        """
    part_of [ @legeos.milestone.m1-session-runtime ]
}

record legeos.work.hands-on-run-2-fixes/1 : work {
    title "Act on the second hands-on run: adjustable windows, visible tiling, body-drag tiles, concise labels, a route to drives, one Settings widget"
    state active
    scope [
        path "apps/lege-files/**",
        path "apps/lege-settings/**",
        path "compositor/lege-comp/**",
        path "crates/lege-types/**",
        path "crates/lege-window/**",
        path "shell/lege-shell/**"
    ]
    intent """
        Fix every deficiency in @legeos.observation.hands-on-run-20260831-findings. (1) Windows are adjustable: the compositor's recovery-band move and corner-grip resize actually start their grabs (they previously demanded an implicit grab that cannot exist yet at band-press time, so both affordances were dead on real hardware). (2) New windows are placed — centred in the usable area, cascaded, size-clamped — instead of honouring a meaningless (0,0) request flush into the corner. (3) Arranging from the Home menu ends the reveal so the result is visible, and arranging with no windows open says so on the field. (4) Object-like tiles (file, folder, pane, app) drag-move from anywhere in their body; instrument tiles keep the band. (5) Browse rows and grids drop the FOLDER/FILE caption noise: the name leads, '/' marks a folder, extensions name files once, folders read as the folder material. (6) The browse toolbar's path is a clickable breadcrumb and a Files button hands the folder to org.legeos.Files with its drives sidebar. (7) The battery/volume/brightness widgets consolidate into ONE Settings widget whose click opens the Settings app, per the user's direct instruction.
        """
    note """
        All seven items are implemented and merged at ad3460b (my commits d79602f..49d999f plus the agent's bf75959..c5a4a0b); every command check passes there and the live nested session confirmed centred placement and oversize clamping. The one open check is #hands-on-confirmation — the user's next login at a real seat: window opens centred, band-move and grip-resize work, tiling menu visibly arranges, tiles drag-move, the Settings widget opens Settings. The packages must be rebuilt and reinstalled first (scripts/reinstall-legeos-desktop.sh, interactive sudo).
        """
    acceptance {
        check body-drag {
            statement """
                Object-like tiles arm a drag from anywhere in their body while widget tiles only grab by their band, and an unmoved press stays a click.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-shell object_tiles_drag_by_their_whole_body_and_instruments_do_not"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.hands-on-2-body-drag-20260831 ]
        }
        check browse-navigation {
            statement """
                The toolbar breadcrumb browses to an ancestor and the Files button hands the open folder to the standalone manager.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-shell -- toolbar_breadcrumb toolbar_files"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.hands-on-2-browse-navigation-20260831 ]
        }
        check gates-green {
            statement """
                The full repository gate passes with all of the above merged.
                """
            method command
            command "just check"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.hands-on-2-gate-20260831 ]
        }
        check hands-on-confirmation {
            statement """
                At a real seat: a new window opens centred and can be moved by its top band and resized by its corner grip; the tiling menu visibly arranges; tiles drag-move; the Settings widget opens Settings.
                """
            method manual
        }
        check placement-policy {
            statement """
                An origin-located map request is centred and cascaded wholly inside the usable area; an oversized one is clamped; a positioned request is honoured and repaired.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-window -- centred cascade clamped honoured"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.hands-on-2-placement-20260831 ]
        }
        check settings-widget {
            statement """
                One Settings widget replaces the battery/volume/brightness tiles, shows their state, and its open action launches the Settings app; saved layouts migrate.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-shell settings"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.settings-widget-consolidation-20260831 ]
        }
    }
    derived_from [ @legeos.observation.hands-on-run-20260831-findings ]
    part_of [ @legeos.work.home-surface-usability-next ]
}

record legeos.work.hands-on-run-3-fixes/1 : work {
    title "Act on the third hands-on run: a usable Files object, a real window frame with controls, and resizable windows"
    state superseded
    scope [
        path "apps/lege-files/**",
        path "compositor/lege-comp/**",
        path "crates/lege-window/**",
        path "debian/control",
        path "shell/lege-shell/**"
    ]
    intent """
        Fix every deficiency in @legeos.observation.hands-on-run-3-findings-20260903 and hand the user a build set they can hot-swap in place. Shell (hot-swappable): (1) a row's first press selects and the second opens, so the selection-gated file verbs have something to act on; (2) Copy path puts the Files.Actions1-rendered text on the clipboard through wl-copy, as the Files app does; (3) a change of reveal state in either direction collapses the expanded Files object; (4) the rail drops PLACE/DRIVE captions, the crumb reads Home ▸ Files, breadcrumb segments are measured not guessed. Files app: the rail names its places once. Compositor (needs a new session): (5) a client window's geometry is its frame and the surface is mapped at and configured to the client area under the band (WindowService::client_area, subtracted in space_sync alone), so the band no longer covers client pixels; (6) the band carries park, maximize and close controls hit-tested against the rectangles chrome draws; (7) a press within RESIZE_MARGIN outside a framed window's edge starts an edge resize, corners included, the window on top first; (8) xdg-decoration is answered ServerSide unless the client insists; (9) a client that commits a size of its own choosing after acking the last configure gets its frame re-fitted, on xdg and X11 alike. Packaging: legeos-shell depends on wl-clipboard.
        """
    note """
        The compositor half cannot be hot-swapped by design (lege-comp.service is Restart=no; lege dev reports it as needs-session). The user must log out and back in for the frame, the controls and the edge resize to appear; the shell and Files app changes take effect on `sudo lege dev deploy`.
        """
    acceptance {
        check band-controls {
            statement """
                Band buttons pack against the right edge in park/maximize/close order, hit-test where they are drawn, and a narrow band keeps close and gives up the rest.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-comp -- band_buttons_pack_against_the_right_edge_close_last a_narrow_band_keeps_close_and_gives_up_the_rest"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.hands-on-3-band-controls-20260903 ]
        }
        check frame-geometry {
            statement """
                client_area sits under the band and frame_around inverts it; resize_edges_at grabs edges only outside the frame, corners included.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-window -- the_client_area_sits_under_the_band edges_are_grabbed_just_outside_the_frame"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.hands-on-3-frame-geometry-20260903 ]
        }
        check gates-green {
            statement """
                The full repository gate passes with all of the above merged.
                """
            method command
            command "just check"
        }
        check hands-on-confirmation {
            statement """
                At a real seat after logout/login: a terminal's first line is visible under its band; the band's close, park and maximize buttons work; a window resizes from its corner grip and from just outside its edges; in the Files object a click selects and the verbs act on the selection; Copy path pastes into a terminal; a bare Super press closes the expanded Files object.
                """
            method manual
        }
        check select-then-open {
            statement """
                In the expanded Files object a row's first press selects it, a second press on the selected row opens it, and search results take the same two presses.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-shell -- file_browser_pointer_activates_folders_and_files file_browser_search_results_use_the_same_clickable_rows"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.hands-on-3-select-then-open-20260903 ]
        }
    }
    derived_from [ @legeos.observation.hands-on-run-3-findings-20260903 ]
    part_of [ @legeos.work.home-surface-usability-next ]
}

record legeos.work.hands-on-run-3-fixes/2 : work {
    title "Act on the third hands-on run: a usable Files object, a real window frame with controls, and resizable windows"
    state active
    scope [
        path "apps/lege-files/**",
        path "compositor/lege-comp/**",
        path "crates/lege-window/**",
        path "debian/control",
        path "shell/lege-shell/**"
    ]
    intent """
        Fix every deficiency in @legeos.observation.hands-on-run-3-findings-20260903 and hand the user a build set they can hot-swap in place. Shell (hot-swappable): (1) a row's first press selects and the second opens, so the selection-gated file verbs have something to act on; (2) Copy path puts the Files.Actions1-rendered text on the clipboard through wl-copy, as the Files app does; (3) a change of reveal state in either direction collapses the expanded Files object; (4) the rail drops PLACE/DRIVE captions, the crumb reads Home ▸ Files, breadcrumb segments are measured not guessed. Files app: the rail names its places once. Compositor (needs a new session): (5) a client window's geometry is its frame and the surface is mapped at and configured to the client area under the band (WindowService::client_area, subtracted in space_sync alone), so the band no longer covers client pixels; (6) the band carries park, maximize and close controls hit-tested against the rectangles chrome draws; (7) a press within RESIZE_MARGIN outside a framed window's edge starts an edge resize, corners included, the window on top first; (8) xdg-decoration is answered ServerSide unless the client insists; (9) a client that commits a size of its own choosing after acking the last configure gets its frame re-fitted, on xdg and X11 alike. Packaging: legeos-shell depends on wl-clipboard.
        """
    note """
        The compositor half cannot be hot-swapped by design (lege-comp.service is Restart=no; lege dev reports it as needs-session). The user must log out and back in for the frame, the controls and the edge resize to appear; the shell and Files app changes take effect on `sudo lege dev deploy`.
        """
    acceptance {
        check band-controls {
            statement """
