record legeos.work.hands-on-run-4-fixes/1 : work {
    title "Act on the fourth hands-on run: a deploy that finishes, snap browsers that connect, per-window compositing, a screen timeout, and a launcher that finds applications"
    state active
    scope [
        path "apps/lege-settings/**",
        path "cli/lege/src/dev/**",
        path "compositor/lege-comp/**",
        path "crates/lege-session-core/**",
        path "distro/deploy/**",
        path "interfaces/**",
        path "services/lege-hostd/**",
        path "services/lege-sessiond/**",
        path "shell/lege-shell/**"
    ]
    intent """
        Fix what the fourth hands-on run found: (1) lege-hostd's EACCES on the system bus socket, and lege dev deploy stopping activation at the first failed unit although every package was installed; (2) snap Chromium and Firefox refused by AppArmor because the public Wayland socket is named legeos-0 rather than wayland-N; (3) every band and grip rendered above every window so titles bleed through a translucent window, plus the reported focus fighting; (4) no screen timeout: a compositor idle timer, outputs off and back on, the timeout from Power1's stored idle policy, and a Settings control; (5) the launcher: sessiond never scanned the snap desktop directory so snap browsers were not in the registry, and the Home field federated files with applications.
        """
    note """
        Landed at 8880b9b. (1) hostd: root cause established by elimination as the ProtectHome=yes mount namespace (the unit had never started; AppArmor in complain mode with zero denials, DAC and bus limits ruled out); ProtectHome dropped, the daemon connects to /run/dbus directly and its failure line now prints uid, socket mode/owner, confinement label and mount namespace; the user can confirm with sudo strace or two systemd-run probes named in the agent report. Deploy runs every activation step and lists every failure. (2) Public socket wayland-0 (new_auto elsewhere); trusted-shell socket legeos-shell-wayland-0, a prefix on purpose because AppArmor's * does not stop at a dash; verified nested with snap Chromium. (3) src/scene.rs builds the frame per window in stacking order, band and grip directly above their own surface; press_target_at is the one hit test and a press on band/grip/edge now activates the window (that was the focus fight). (4) src/idle.rs plus lege_shell_v1 v4 set_idle_timeout, DrmCompositor::clear for DPMS off, Settings System page control from Never to 30 minutes, Power1 documents which field is enforced. (5) d391fc1, dfa1fda. Compositor, hostd and socket changes need a logout; hostd needs the deploy's system-unit restart.
        """
    acceptance {
        check gates-green {
            statement """
                just check exits 0 at the merged branch
                """
            method command
            command "just check"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.hands-on-4-gate-20260903 ]
        }
        check hostd-starts {
            statement """
                After deploy, lege-hostd.service is active and lege dev deploy activates every component
                """
            method manual
        }
        check launcher-finds-snap-apps {
            statement """
                The registry scans the snap desktop directory and the Home field offers applications only
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-sessiond && cargo test -p lege-shell"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.hands-on-4-launcher-20260903 ]
        }
        check per-window-compositing {
            statement """
                A window behind a translucent Kitty shows through at Kitty's opacity, and a click on any band or grip focuses that window
                """
            method manual
        }
        check screen-timeout {
            statement """
                Settings › System shows Screen turns off after; the screen turns off after the chosen idle time and back on at the next input
                """
            method manual
        }
        check snap-browsers-connect {
            statement """
                After logout and login, snap Chromium and Firefox open on the Wayland display
                """
            method manual
        }
    }
    after [ @legeos.work.hands-on-run-3-fixes ]
    part_of [ @legeos.work.home-surface-usability-next ]
}

record legeos.work.hands-on-run-5-fixes/1 : work {
    title "Act on the fifth hands-on run: folder windows instead of one full-screen file manager, Home not drawn under windows, a finer grid and icons where words repeated"
    state active
    scope [ path "shell/lege-shell/**" ]
    intent """
        Turn the fifth hands-on run's findings into Home Field behaviour, reusing the tile system rather than adding a second windowing system inside the shell. A folder tile becomes a window that lists its directory and can be moved, resized, grouped and reopened like any tile; typing a path opens one; the XDG Desktop folder opens as a small tray that a press expands; the Files object becomes a window over Home rather than Home becoming a file manager; the field paints flat ground over every window's rectangle so nothing of Home shows through a translucent client; the grid cell drops from 104 to 88 logical pixels; and the Files rail draws theme icons instead of repeating the word 'folder' under every folder name.
        """
    note """
        The empty-space finding is only partly addressed: folder tiles now carry content instead of a dim path, but no whole-field layout policy was written, and a default Home is still mostly ground. That is a separate decision about what Home is for when it is empty.
        """
    acceptance {
        check desktop-tray {
            statement """
                The XDG Desktop folder is placed at the folder kind's floor and a press is what grows it
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-shell --lib desktop_folder_opens"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.hands-on-5-gate-20260904 ]
        }
        check folder-windows {
            statement """
                A folder tile lists its directory, opens once per path, and is an ordinary placeable tile
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-shell --lib folder_window_opens"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.hands-on-5-gate-20260904 ]
        }
        check hands-on-confirmation {
            statement """
                On the installed desktop: two folder windows open at once, a translucent kitty shows no trace of Home through it, the Desktop tray expands and collapses, and the Files rail shows icons rather than the word 'folder' twice
                """
            method manual
        }
        check no-home-under-windows {
            statement """
                Nothing of Home is drawn where an un-shelved window is, and Home in the gaps between windows is untouched
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-shell --lib a_windows_rectangle"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.hands-on-5-gate-20260904 ]
        }
        check preview-capture-stops {
            statement """
                Preview capture stops while a fullscreen or maximized window covers the field and resumes on reveal, park or un-maximize, with the cache kept
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-shell --lib a_window_covering"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.hands-on-5-gate-20260904 ]
        }
        check shell-gate {
            statement """
                The shell crate is green: rustfmt, clippy pedantic with warnings denied, and every test
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-shell && cargo clippy -p lege-shell --all-targets"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.hands-on-5-gate-20260904 ]
        }
        check typed-path-opens-a-window {
            statement """
                A typed absolute or ~-relative path is read as a path and offered as the first omnibox row
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-shell --lib a_typed_path"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.hands-on-5-gate-20260904 ]
        }
    }
    derived_from [ @legeos.observation.hands-on-run-5-findings-20260904 ]
    part_of [ @legeos.work.home-surface-usability-next ]
}

record legeos.work.home-developer-setup-preview/1 : work {
    title "Proposal: an optional, previewed Home setup for development"
    state proposed
    intent """
        For later consideration, offer an explicit setup action that previews a small developer working set built from existing Home objects: chosen project folder windows, project tiles and pinned editor/terminal providers. Let the person choose paths and remove suggested items before applying. Apply as one undoable layout operation, preserve existing geometry, and retain useful drop space. Never scan repositories automatically, infer projects from proximity, repack on activity, or turn Home into persistent application chrome. This is an extrapolation from the unresolved default-empty-field finding, not an accepted replacement layout.
        """
    note """
        No implementation in the 2026-09-05 review. Decide whether this belongs in first-run, Settings, or the Home menu before implementing; avoid adding a second application inventory.
        """
    acceptance {
        check explicit-preview {
            statement """
                A person reviews and edits the suggested objects and paths before a single apply; cancel changes nothing and Undo restores the previous field.
                """
            method manual
        }
        check stable-existing-work {
            statement """
                Applying the suggestion leaves existing tile geometry unchanged; overflow is explicit and no filesystem objects are moved or deleted.
                """
            method command
        }
    }
    part_of [ @legeos.work.home-surface-usability-next ]
}

record legeos.work.home-field/1 : work {
    title "Home Field — taskbar-free desktop surface: tiles, parked sessions, go-home, information row, projects and previews"
    state active
    scope [
        path "compositor/**",
        path "crates/lege-field/**",
        path "crates/lege-session-core/**",
        path "crates/lege-treemap/**",
        path "crates/lege-window/**",
        path "interfaces/**",
        path "services/lege-sessiond/**",
        path "shell/**"
    ]
    intent """
        Replace the drawer-list Home Surface with the Home Field: a bounded, taskbar-free field of rectangular tiles (projects, active apps / parked sessions, file trays, widgets, system) on the shell's Layer::HomeSurface backdrop. Installed-but-idle desktop entries remain searchable instead of automatically covering the field. Windows collapse into tiles instead of minimising and expand back out; a bare Super tap is the primary temporary Home toggle, with Ctrl+Alt+H and Super+D retained as fallbacks, and the reveal changes no window state. A standard information row on Home begins with local date/time, live/parked counts, and the selected network-status provider, using nm-tray2 for network control. Dragging a tile onto a target performs a typed, previewed, undoable operation; layout is a stable local grid that never reflows globally, persisted per output by sessiond (org.legeos.HomeField1). Phases: 1 compositor truths (shelved windows actually hidden and not hit-tested, maximize, reveal-home command + keybindings + protocol v2 with identifier/geometry), 2 the pure crates/lege-field model (document, ops with inverses, local reflow, representation ladder, drag/throw state machine), 3 FieldScreen in lege-shell with --print field and full keyboard reach, 4 HomeField1 persistence, 5 projects/trays/zoom, 6 previews over ext-image-copy-capture, 7 lege-treemap and budgeted widgets, 8 the throw spike with a keep/delete rule. Plan of record: ~/.claude/plans/for-this-project-i-crispy-shannon.md (author's machine).
        """
    note """
        Decisions taken with the author on 2026-08-22: Super+D is a temporary reveal, not park-all; one field document per output, primary output first; LegeOS and Silvaview-rs relicensed AGPL-3.0-only (D13) so lege-treemap can be lifted. Reveal state is a view flag in WindowService; one lege-field crate is the single model for shell and sessiond, Ctrl+Z is HomeField1.Undo.
        """
    acceptance {
        check field-in-text {
            statement """
                lege-shell --print field lists exactly the tiles the graphical field draws, one line per tile.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-shell print_field"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.home-field-command-checks-20260831/1 ]
        }
        check field-is-keyboard-complete {
            statement """
                Every Home Field action reachable by pointer is reachable by keyboard alone (arrows, Enter, Space, Escape, Ctrl+Z).
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-shell field_keyboard"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.home-field-command-checks-20260831/1 ]
        }
        check home-is-always-reachable {
            statement """
                A bare Super tap is the primary Home toggle; Ctrl+Alt+H, Super+D and Home's own button reach the same taskbar-free reveal with every client window hidden, and Escape, pressing again, or activating a window restores the exact prior stack.
                """
            method manual
        }
        check layout-is-stable {
            statement """
                Content, title, state or count changes move zero tiles; an insert displaces only tiles in the affected row, column or container; every field op's inverse restores the document exactly.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-field"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.home-field-command-checks-20260831/1 ]
        }
        check maximize-fills-work-area {
            statement """
                Maximizing fills exactly one output's usable area, with no built-in taskbar reservation, and remains recoverable for any topology; unmaximize restores the floating geometry.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-window maximize"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.home-field-command-checks-20260831/1 ]
        }
        check no-new-toolkit-api {
            statement """
                just check passes with ../pixelkit unmodified; the Home Field needed no pixelkit API change.
                """
            method command
            command "just check"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.home-field-command-checks-20260831/1 ]
        }
        check reveal-survives-shell-death {
            statement """
                Killing lege-shell while a reveal is in effect ends the reveal: every window reappears without user action.
                """
            method manual
        }
        check shelved-is-hidden {
            statement """
                A shelved (minimised) window is unmapped from the compositor's Space: it neither renders nor receives pointer input, and its recovery band is not painted; unshelving restores it at its repaired geometry.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-window -p lege-comp shelving_hides_and_unshelving_shows"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.home-field-command-checks-20260831/1 ]
        }
        check windows-cannot-be-lost {
            statement """
                No sequence of shelve, reveal-home, activate or maximize leaves a window neither visible nor unshelvable; show-every-window unshelves everything; a reveal changes no window record.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-window -- hidden_windows_are_explained_by_shelf_or_reveal_alone show_all_windows_unshelves_everything_and_ends_a_reveal a_reveal_changes_no_window_and_ends_on_activate"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.home-field-command-checks-20260831/1 ]
        }
    }
    depends_on [ @legeos.decision.agplv3-own-code, @legeos.decision.compositor-on-smithay ]
    implements [
        @legeos.constraint.packaging-and-render-thread,
        @legeos.constraint.services-not-indicators
    ]
    part_of [ @legeos.milestone.m2-session-runs ]
}

record legeos.work.home-field-discoverability/1 : work {
    title "Render the cheat sheet the action manifest can already generate, and give the pointer-only actions a chord"
    state completed
    scope [ path "crates/lege-types/**", path "shell/lege-shell/**" ]
    intent """
        Nothing about the Home Field is discoverable. There is no cheat sheet, no help overlay, no tooltip, no first-run — grepping the shell for cheat, help, shortcut, onboarding, tooltip and first-run finds only doc comments describing a cheat sheet that would read the action manifest, and a backend data migration named first_run that no user ever sees. The only hints in the product are the accelerator beside each context-menu row, an Escape breadcrumb while a drawer is expanded, and the search placeholder.

        This compounds every other divergence. A user who has lost the taskbar and the virtual desktops has to find park, show-all and restore to work at all, and those actions carry chords: &[] in the manifest (crates/lege-types/src/action.rs:338-515) — window.park, window.close, field.restore, field.reset and every session.* verb are reachable only by guessing that a right-click menu exists on a surface with no visible affordance for one. The audit's verdict on the one-workspace invariant turns entirely on this: the substitute for virtual desktops is sound, and undiscoverable.

        Two halves. First, render a cheat sheet from the manifest — the declaration already exists and check-actions already enforces that every action a surface performs is declared, so this is a view over data the project maintains, not a new list to keep in sync. Second, decide chords for the actions that have none, which is a design call about which verbs earn a key rather than a mechanical fill-in.
        """
    note """
        Rank 2 of the audit's daily-work gaps. The manifest already carries everything a cheat sheet needs; nothing renders it.
        """
    depends_on [ @legeos.work.action-manifest-one-declaration-three-surfaces ]
    derived_from [ @legeos.assessment.home-field-usability-gaps-20260831 ]
    part_of [ @legeos.work.home-field ]
}

record legeos.work.home-field-selection-and-bulk-action/1 : work {
    title "A selection, not just a focus — so more than one thing can be acted on at once"
    state completed
    scope [ path "crates/lege-field/**", path "shell/lege-shell/**" ]
    intent """
        The Home Field has no selection at all, only a focus: a single focus: Option<TileId> (shell/lege-shell/src/surface/field_screen.rs:157), and a single entry_focus: usize in the drawer browser (surface/file_browser.rs:54). Every keyboard and pointer path that looks like selecting overwrites that one field. There is no shift-click, no ctrl-click, no marquee, and consequently no way to move three files, trash a group of downloads, or stash several tiles — each is one item at a time or not at all. Drag carries a single TileId by construction (crates/lege-field/src/drag.rs:52), and FieldOp::Move, Resize and Stash each take one id.

        Ranked first because it is the plainest daily-work blocker in the audit: bulk action is table stakes everywhere else, and its absence is felt on the ordinary path rather than an exotic one.

        The work is a model change before it is a UI one. lege-field is where selection has to live to keep the ops invertible — a bulk move must be one undoable op, not N ops that undo one at a time — so expect FieldOp variants that take a set, and the existing property tests (ops_keep_invariants_and_invert_exactly, placing_moves_only_band_mates) to be the gate on getting it right. Shift-click for a range, ctrl-click to toggle, drag-on-background for a marquee, and Ctrl+A; keyboard parity means shift-arrows extending the selection, since the field is deliberately keyboard-complete.
        """
    note """
        Rank 1 of the audit's daily-work gaps. The lege-field invariant tests are the reason to do the model first: a bulk op that does not invert exactly would break a property the field already guarantees.
        """
    derived_from [ @legeos.assessment.home-field-usability-gaps-20260831 ]
    part_of [ @legeos.work.home-field ]
}

record legeos.work.home-field-settings-gui/1 : work {
    title "Graphical Settings for displays, mouse/trackpad and Home appearance"
    state proposed
    scope [
        path "apps/lege-settings/**",
        path "compositor/lege-comp/**",
        path "crates/lege-session-core/src/settings.rs",
        path "interfaces/dbus/**",
        path "services/lege-sessiond/**",
        path "shell/lege-shell/src/surface/design.rs"
    ]
    intent """
        The graphical Settings app already edits the five Home Field tuning keys; replace the vague goal of making every read-only diagnostic tab editable with the common controls needed for daily use.

        Displays: enumerate connected outputs and allow resolution, refresh rate, rotation/orientation and scale per output, including mixed-scale arrangements. Apply through compositor-owned validated configuration with a visible confirmation countdown and automatic rollback when the new mode is not confirmed or the output disappears. Show the resulting logical arrangement before applying and retain a known-good configuration.

        Mouse and trackpad: expose pointer speed, acceleration profile, natural scrolling, primary-button choice and scroll behaviour; for touchpads also tap-to-click, tap-and-drag, two-finger/edge scrolling and disable-while-typing where libinput supports them. Unsupported controls are identified as unavailable rather than drawn as inert switches.

        Appearance: select light/dark or bundled themes, accent and object-material palette/texture roles, background/wallpaper behaviour, and the defaults used by Home panels, folder panes and widgets. Themes are declarative design tokens/material assets, never executable shell extensions, and application fullscreen remains free of Home chrome. Every graphical setting writes through a typed service/schema and has Reset; CLI inspection/change remains equivalent. Provider, association, history and hardware diagnostic pages may remain read-only until their own scoped work exists.
        """
    note """
        Two design questions surveyed on 2026-08-31, to settle before implementation. (1) Channel: display and libinput configuration are compositor-owned, but lege-comp deliberately speaks no D-Bus and the Settings app is not the trusted-shell client; the candidate routes are a second privileged Wayland protocol on the trusted socket relayed by the shell, or sessiond mediating over a new compositor-side channel — either way interfaces/ first, and the winit backend cannot modeset, so the display half is udev-backend-only with an honest degradation nested. (2) Appearance: shell/lege-shell/src/surface/design.rs is compile-time constants referenced throughout the painters; light/dark/accent/material as declarative tokens means making that module palette-driven first — a mechanical but wide refactor that should be its own commit ahead of any Settings UI. The visual-regression baseline must be re-reviewed when the default palette is touched.
        """
    acceptance {
        check mixed-scale-preview {
            statement """
                Settings previews the logical mixed-scale output arrangement accurately and applying it keeps every window recoverable.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-window -p lege-settings display"
        }
        check mouse-trackpad-controls {
            statement """
                Mouse and touchpad settings map to the correct libinput devices, persist independently, and unsupported capabilities render explicitly unavailable rather than inert.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-comp -p lege-settings input_settings"
        }
        check safe-display-configuration {
            statement """
                Resolution, refresh, rotation and per-output scale validate against live modes; an unconfirmed, failed or disconnected-output apply automatically restores the known-good topology.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-comp display_configuration"
        }
        check theme-and-material-tokens {
            statement """
                Light/dark, accent, background and object-material choices update Home through declarative validated tokens/assets, persist, reset, and cannot load executable shell code.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-shell -p lege-settings appearance"
        }
        check typed-service-parity {
            statement """
                Every graphical control is represented by a typed schema/service value with validation, CLI parity and a Reset path.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-session-core -p lege-settings && cargo run -q -p xtask -- check-interfaces"
        }
    }
    depends_on [
        @legeos.constraint.services-not-indicators,
        @legeos.work.file-operations-from-home,
        @legeos.work.home-file-sorting-and-view-modes,
        @legeos.work.home-panel-and-dock-layouts,
        @legeos.work.reversible-window-arrangement-presets
    ]
    derived_from [ @legeos.assessment.home-field-usability-gaps-20260831 ]
    implements [ @legeos.decision.home-is-momentary-and-placeable-objects-are-containers ]
    part_of [ @legeos.work.home-surface-usability-next ]
}

record legeos.work.home-file-sorting-and-view-modes/1 : work {
    title "Folder sorting plus list and thumbnail modes across Home and Files"
    state completed
    scope [
        path "apps/lege-files/**",
        path "crates/lege-client/**",
        path "services/lege-filed/**",
        path "shell/lege-shell/**"
    ]
    intent """
        Give every Home folder/shortcut pane and the standalone Files app an explicit presentation control. List mode shows name, type, size and modified time with bounded columns. Thumbnail mode lays out responsive preview cells using Files.Previews1 and the same representation ladder, request limits and off-thread decoding already used by the inspector. Switching modes preserves selection, focus and the nearest visible item rather than jumping to the top.

        Offer deterministic sorting by natural name, type, size and modified time in ascending or descending order, with a clear folder-first choice and stable tie breakers. A shortcut pane may additionally retain its manual reference order. Home and Files share one sort descriptor/comparator contract so the same directory never silently changes order between surfaces. Store a global default plus per-folder/pane overrides, and expose every choice by pointer and keyboard. Thumbnails remain content inside a folder/pane; they do not become loose Home tiles.
        """
    acceptance {
        check bounded-preview-loading {
            statement """
                Thumbnail mode requests only visible/near-visible bounded previews, cancels stale requests and never decodes or walks files on the render thread.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-shell -p lege-files thumbnail"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.file-sorting-and-view-modes-20260831/1 ]
        }
        check list-and-thumbnail {
            statement """
                Both Home folder surfaces and Files can switch between bounded detail-list and responsive thumbnail modes without losing selection, focus or scroll context.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-shell -p lege-files view_mode"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.file-sorting-and-view-modes-20260831/1 ]
        }
        check no-loose-thumbnail-tiles {
            statement """
                Thumbnail cells exist only inside folder or shortcut-pane surfaces and cannot be persisted as loose Home file tiles.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-field -p lege-shell no_loose_file_tiles"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.file-sorting-and-view-modes-20260831/1 ]
        }
        check preferences-persist {
            statement """
                Global defaults and per-folder/pane sort/view overrides round-trip, survive restart and reset independently.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-session-core file_view_preferences"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.file-sorting-and-view-modes-20260831/1 ]
        }
        check sort-contract {
            statement """
                Natural name, type, size, modified and manual-reference sorts are deterministic total orders with stable tie breakers, ascending/descending handling and an explicit folder-first policy shared by Home and Files.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-filed -p lege-files sort"
            verified_by [ @legeos.evidence.file-sorting-and-view-modes-20260831/1 ]
        }
    }
    depends_on [ @legeos.work.home-folders-and-shortcut-panes ]
    implements [ @legeos.decision.home-is-momentary-and-placeable-objects-are-containers ]
    part_of [ @legeos.work.home-surface-usability-next ]
}

record legeos.work.home-file-surface/1 : work {
    title "Home file surface — real drive-backed contents, clickable navigation and brokered file opening"
    state superseded
    scope [
        path "crates/lege-client/**",
        path "docs/architecture/files.md",
        path "interfaces/dbus/org.legeos.Files.*",
        path "services/lege-filed/**",
        path "shell/lege-shell/**"
    ]
    intent """
        Replace Home's text-only folder and drive panes with a bounded structured browser backed by lege-filed. Expanded file panes show actual entries from XDG folders and user-visible mounted volumes, directory rows navigate by pointer and keyboard, file rows resolve and launch through Associations1 and Launcher1, and Home remains the taskbar-free open-window/process overview reached by a bare Super tap. Use the existing Silvaview-derived treemap code for space composition only; its size-descending treemap ordering is not the list-view policy.
        """
    note """
        This is the immediately usable integrated Home file surface. The unpinned COSMIC Files fork remains the eventual full standalone manager for rename/copy/property workflows; this pass must not make Home depend on that absent binary.
        """
    acceptance {
        check brokered-file-opening {
            statement """
                Home opens a selected file only by resolving Associations1 then launching the returned canonical AppId through Launcher1, and reports an unresolved association without bypassing policy.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-shell brokered_file_open"
        }
        check clickable-file-panes {
            statement """
                Expanded Home folder and drive panes render actual service entries; pointer and keyboard activation navigate directories and request file opening, with back/up and drive-root navigation.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-shell file_browser"
        }
        check home-window-overview-preserved {
            statement """
                Every compositor toplevel remains represented on Home and the bare-Super tap/reveal path remains the taskbar-free route to see all open windows at once.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-shell field_model && cargo test -p lege-comp keybindings::tests"
        }
        check structured-directory-data {
            statement """
                lege-filed exposes bounded structured directory entries with deterministic folder-first natural-name ordering, including hidden/symlink/type/size/mtime metadata and clear errors.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo test -p lege-filed browse"
        }
        check workspace-verifies {
            statement """
                Formatting, warnings-denied clippy, workspace tests and interface consistency checks pass.
                """
            method command
            command "cargo fmt --all -- --check && cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings && cargo test --workspace && cargo xtask check-interfaces"
        }
    }
    implements [ @legeos.constraint.services-not-indicators/1 ]
    part_of [ @legeos.work.home-field/1 ]
    supported_by [ @legeos.observation.hardware-home-loads-but-file-panes-empty/1 ]
}

